# OpenSpec workflow (MVDS)

Copied/adapted from experiment-hub. Schema SoT for this repo: [`openspec/schemas/mvds-default/`](../openspec/schemas/mvds-default/) (default; [`experiment-hub-lite`](../openspec/schemas/experiment-hub-lite/) is the archived hub mirror, selectable per-change).

## When to use

- **mvds-default** (default): Human anchor, Outcomes, specs (≤5 requirements), **discovery** (0.0 As-is → 0.5 Eval → 0.6 Eval Summary — founder stop before any proposal), design (1.0 conditioned on the summary; Figma table for UI; 1.5 Eval Delta, informational), tasks §1 = user scenarios. `/opsx:propose` creates **one artifact per approval**.
- **Cursor-only plans** are fine for tiny chores; use OpenSpec when you want durable proposal/design/tasks and Figma iteration before code.
- Do **not** invent `bhd-experiment` or full `experiment-hub` schemas until they are copied into this repo.

## Git discipline

Match [github-workflow.mdc](github-workflow.mdc) and AGENTS.md Branch & PR workflow: one feature branch, draft PR, founder merges. Align change folder name with the branch when practical (`feat/storybook-start-here` ↔ `openspec/changes/storybook-start-here/`).

**`/opsx:apply`:** Implement tasks; when apply finishes, commit + push + draft PR per schema `apply.instruction` and [`skills/openspec-apply-change.md`](../skills/openspec-apply-change.md). **`/opsx:propose`** does not commit.

## Scope pivots

When the founder redirects a change's scope mid-flight (e.g. "restyle the panel" becomes "remove the panel"):

- **Rename the change directory** to describe what the change now does (`git mv openspec/changes/<old> openspec/changes/<new>`) — the change id should stay truthful, not historical.
- **Rewrite the proposal** to the new scope, quoting the redirecting sentence **verbatim** as the new (or leading) Human anchor — the pivot instruction is founder intent, and the anchor is where founder intent lives.
- **Record the pivot in the proposal**, one or two lines: what it began as, what redirected it, and where superseded work lives (Figma pages, docs) so nothing explored is lost.
- **Retitle/re-body the open PR** to match. Superseded design artifacts stay in their file as a parked record — not deleted. Prior Figma pages are never overwritten (see [figma.mdc](figma.mdc) page convention).

Ported from experiment-hub (precedent: `method-page` → `remove-workflow-page`, 2026-07-21).

## Figma and `design.md`

UI-impacting changes MUST produce a Figma **as-is + proposed** pair and record it in `design.md` — not skippable, and **removals count as UI changes** (see [figma.mdc](figma.mdc)). Map to MVDS tokens/components. Library sync to MVDS Core only when the founder asks.

